- Alright, let's close
out with a great story

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.000
from the world of social media.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.619
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.619 --> 00:00:10.260
(upbeat music)
(cheering)

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.080
So it's dry January, the
time after the holidays

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.180
when people try to cut back on alcohol.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.620
Good luck Shelton.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.890
But cutting back doesn't mean
you can't enjoy a night out.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.130
Here in Manhattan there's a bar
dedicated to sober drinking.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.130
It's called Hekate, and they
even serve craft mocktails.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.699
Super cool.

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:28.532
We have the owner on the line.

00:00:28.532 --> 00:00:31.440
Say hi to Abby who watches
on NBC New York everybody.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.343
What's up Abby?

00:00:33.821 --> 00:00:35.280
- Hi.
(cheering)

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:36.210
- Hi!

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.580
So you say it's a great time to be sober.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.413
Why?

00:00:39.413 --> 00:00:42.090
- It's actually the best
time in history to be sober

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.640
because there are
hundreds of products now,

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.170
not just one near beer,

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.420
but hundreds of alcohol free products

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.060
designed just for people
who've given up alcohol.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.250
- You're totally, I remember
when I was a waitress, oh,

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.100
many years ago, it was
like Buckley or Buckler.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.690
There was like this one beer.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.120
Yeah, yeah, there was this
one beer you could get, yeah.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.070
I was like, oh man, you're driving.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.480
I was like, anyway.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:05.181
Well, what's on the menu?

00:01:05.181 --> 00:01:07.440
- We've got all kinds of delicious things.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.670
Our bestseller is the Healer,
which see how purple it is.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.010
People love to put that on Instagram.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.460
And that doesn't try to
be any alcoholic beverage.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.000
It's not imitating an
alcohol-free beverage.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.980
We do have spicy margaritas
and virgin pina coladas.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.050
So there are drinks you'll recognize

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.910
from being in a regular bar.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:32.106
And then we have a lot
of products that are just

00:01:32.106 --> 00:01:34.200
stand on their own as something

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.910
that never had alcohol at all.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.320
- Yeah, fancy fun drinks.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:38.250
I like it.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.870
That's fun, it looked like a fun drink.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.520
Looked like a good time in a cup.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.860
Well, thank you so much,
Abby, this is so cool.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:46.140
And also it makes it easier, a
lot of friends that are sober

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.060
and it makes it cool for
them to go and hang out

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.770
and still have a good
time and still feel like

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.513
they're like a part of it in
the same way, that's very cool.

00:01:51.513 --> 00:01:53.370
- That's why I opened the bar.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:56.190
It was, I have a regular
bar right across the street

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.150
and a couple of my real,
real regular customers

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.180
gave up alcohol for
sordid and sundry reasons

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.520
and I thought well, I
need to create a place

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.610
where there's a sense of
community and a sense of fun,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.250
but where there isn't the
temptation of alcohol.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.200
So that's what this is for.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.033
- Oh, that's super cool.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.060
Thank you so much, Abby.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.610
I'm liking your post right now.

